# AI Studio Colab operator (Cursor adapter)

Read [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) for durable, editor-neutral operating authority.
It and newer accepted architecture decisions take precedence over this adapter
and older operational examples. This adapter grants no execution or review authority.

For task-authorized Cursor/browser/Colab work, follow the
[operator runbook](../../docs/cursor-colab-operator.md). It contains the lifecycle,
Chrome/CDP, menu, checkpoint reporting, and cancellation procedures.

Cursor-specific reminders:

- Capture a RUNNING `operator_run_id` using the runbook's `begin` procedure before
  Chrome or helper work; use the gated Chrome launcher.
- Run long-lived `_checkpoint_*`, `_probe_*`, `_diag_*`, `_status_*`, and similar
  helpers through `run-helper`, keeping the containment parent alive. Do not run
  them directly in an Agent terminal or detach a spawn-and-exit wrapper.
- Prefer background CDP and semantic labels; verify each menu title before the
  next selection. Do not force desktop focus for routine operator work.
- For notebook source entry, use the runbook's CDP cell primitive and verify
  `getText()` after `setText()`; never append at the current caret.
- Cursor UI Stop may skip Python cleanup hooks. Follow the runbook's explicit
  stop/status procedure when possible and report cleanup limitations.

Identity, service permissions, execution gates, Git/review/acceptance rules, and
architecture conflict handling are defined in AGENTS.md, not independently here.
